    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Regarding the kiln atmosphere, if I'm seeing clusters of these spots rather than uniform discoloration, would that more likely point to a specific stage in the firing process, like a sudden reduction period, or is it possible the shards were just poorly organized in the kiln pit? I'm trying to figure out if the distribution pattern tells us anything about the scale of the workshop.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
